        "title": "Along the river...we leave the body",
        "text": "Imagine a river, low water and quiet one (Bagmati, not basmati). \nOld buildings, palm readers, monkeys. Smoke, long hair ashes covered Sadhus and Spirit. Dictionary said spirit is a being separate from the body, and that many religions believe continue to exist after the body dies or even the form of a dead person, similar to a ghost, or the feeling that a dead person is present although you cannot see them.\nPashupatinath is the hindu place where bodies are burned in order to set free the soul of deaths. Very mystical location where you should watch and elaborate life's meaning.\n\nYou should take a look as a living ghost, respecting people mourning.\nImportant Hindu temple adjacent, not open for not hindus!",
